From 1d34c4f23befa19b10170d11af040240f6a57937 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 09:45:28 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 11259/11362] Key exhaustion by the supervisor's own stretch,
 with the enabled set read at the row (REQ-ARC-WMTE-7033 rule 6)

Round four, after the adversarial review of cff7630c6a. Two findings
blocked, both the same species as the defect round three fixed: a reader
deriving from run-level aggregates what only the producer knows at the
moment of the window.

Finding 1 (live). `observe` clears the spent set only on a MONOTONE level
increase (`snapshot.level > self._last_level`), but the window row wrote
the raw `level` and the reader grouped on it. The raw counter falls on a
full reset while the spent set does not clear (cd82 in
cd82-r11l-727651.json: 0->1 at frame 770, 1->0 at 873, 0->1 at 1512,
1->0 at 1615), so two stretches merged into one cell and
`windows_on_level`, `arms_fired_on_level`, `level_resolved_by_levelup`
and `actions_from_first_exhaustion_to_levelup` were computed over
different spans than `exhausted_windows`.

Finding 9 (latent). `enabled_arms_for_entry` unions arms fired anywhere
in the run, so a tool rung fired on stretch 5 after an env flip raised
the bar for a stretch-2 window that could never have fired it.

One producer edit resolves both. `_record_unredirected_window` now writes
`stretch_level` (`_last_level`: moves only on a level-up, the same moment
`_arms_used` clears) and `arms_enabled` (`enabled_arms()` read at the
window); redirect rows carry `stretch_level` too. The reader groups by
`stretch_level`, tests `row.arms_enabled <= row.arms_used` per row (a row
without its own set falls back to the receipt-level set, so REQ-7030's
reader stays live), and lists a receipt whose rows lack `stretch_level`
as not decidable (`window_rows_lack_stretch_level`) instead of keying it
by the raw level. exp6921 passes `stretch_level` through its corrected
redirects.

Also from the review: receipt totals on a cell are renamed
`stagnations_unredirected_receipt_total` / `windows_dropped_receipt_total`
(finding 5); the report says "no UNSPENT arm was left", not "every arm
spent", and a new WINDOWS RECORDED section prints every receipt's window
summary so windows with unspent-but-ineligible arms are visible
(finding 3; gives `exhaustion_summary` its production caller, finding 8);
the untagged test now names SCENARIO-7030-B (finding 6); exp6921's test
asserts `arms_enabled_source == "receipt"` and the dropped total, and a new
case (declared four, spent three -> no row) makes the receipt-level
pass-through bite (finding 4).

Tests: 133 pass across the eight affected files. New: 7033-E (the real
cd82 timeline replayed through the real supervisor: one cell on stretch 0,
3 windows, resolved 291 actions later; ten stretch-1 rows read raw level 0
and stay out of it), a hand-built dip, 7033-F (row-level enabled set),
7033-G (window summaries), rows-without-stretch listed. The mutation
proof follows in the next commit with the spec.

Pre-existing, not touched here: two tests in
test_experiment_6558_arc_live_redirect_ledger_reachability.py fail on
this tree and fail identically with the supervisor and the refinement
module restored to HEAD and to the merge base (exp6558 imports only
`ARM_ORDER` from the supervisor, which did not change).

